@@ -1,5 +1,18 @@
 ## [Unreleased]

+### Added
+
+- Home cover grid browses all retained opened books from a compact SD ordering, without the old 18-book ceiling. It reuses Library thumbnail identities, cover pixels and the background conversion worker; visible covers load first and later history pages prepare while idle. Existing recent entries migrate automatically.
+
+- Library cover view uses the same three-column cover component, proportions and frames as Home, without book-name labels. Cover conversion runs on a low-priority disk-only worker, preparing visible books first and then other pages while idle. Swipes cancel taps before paging; holding a cover keeps the existing book menu. Display settings separate All books, Recently opened and List grouping. Library filters progress after the first paint instead of blocking entry; index reads reuse SD sectors rather than issuing a small read per folder.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Marking a book finished updates Library rows without restarting its filter; shifted history indices no longer leave stale covers. Swipes suppress delayed taps and physical page buttons page cover views. Home cover grid swipes through all retained reading history while keeping the current book featured.
+
+- Library cover view keeps its 3 × 3 grid while moving sorting into the menu and combining counts/pages in one compact footer. Covers use tight centered gaps, retain painted pixels, and update as a batch. Completed filtered/recent views are cached on SD, so returning to an unchanged library restores counts without rescanning. Missing covers show the book title inside a book outline; “Refresh covers on this page” retries those nine covers.
+
+- Library opens its saved index without an unconditional cold-boot scan and caches folder offsets for book lookups. Repeated missing-file checks no longer block opening the library. Transfers and detected SD file changes offer Refresh without blocking the saved library; a missing or incompatible index still requires an initial scan.

 - Image refresh blanks each image separately, keeping text between inline images visible while images are prepared for display. Pending images use an empty background instead of a temporary box border.

@@ -39,6 +52,7 @@
 - TTF font support on ESP32-S3 devices. Whole-point sizes from 8pt to 22pt will be automatically available.
 - Separate saved highlights retain clear side/top/bottom gutters, while each highlight stays continuous across its wrapped lines. Extending a saved highlight into another by at least one complete word merges their text and records on commit, including chained overlaps. Drag release and editor Save use the same atomic merge; adjacency, punctuation-only contact, Cancel and unchanged drafts do not merge.
 - Newly created highlights now share the same one-word overlap merge as edited highlights. Saved highlights show same-shade, full-height continuation triangles toward the next/previous page. Separate quotes keep a visible horizontal gap even when tight line spacing overlaps their line boxes; wrapped rows within one quote remain joined.
+- The end-of-book screen now has a touch close button and supports backward swipes to return to the last page. Dismissing it cancels the automatic Finished-folder move and restores the recent-book entry.
 - Readest sync retries a rejected session once after refreshing its token, without replaying server failures. Errors now show the failing operation and HTTP status instead of an unexplained server-error message.
 - Readest sign-in and token refresh now use Readest's permanent Supabase project address, matching upstream's migration away from the old vanity host.
 - Horizontal gaps between separate highlights are now five pixels, taking the extra space from the lower highlight only where needed. Grey highlight boxes now stay visually separate when two quotes share a line and wrap above/below one another. Ownership-aware stepped boundaries prevent background overlap around the side gap while each individual quote remains continuous, including tight spacing and right-to-left layouts.
